Adversarially review the drafts of a research document. Cover: factual grounding (claims not
supported by evidence), balance and steelmanning of opposing views, coverage gaps, structure and
coherence, redundancy, unsupported novelty claims, and style.

For each problem produce an Issue with: a stable id, severity (info|minor|major|blocking),
category, the target section id, a concrete description, and supporting evidence. Rank the most
serious first. Only raise an issue that requires a change; do not invent problems. If the drafts
are sound, return an empty issues list.

